title: Bonfire - Cooperative Hosting Network
description: An open invitation to assemble a co-operative ecosystem to operate a sustainable, resilient infrastructure for Bonfire development, hosting, and technical support.
---
{# ============================================================
   V2 · HOSTING — cooperative hosting network (Tailwind + daisyUI)
   Same content as before, v2 skin.
   ============================================================ #}
{% set eyebrow = "flex items-center gap-3 font-smono text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-[.18em] uppercase" %}
{% set display = "mt-4 font-disp font-[560] text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.3rem)] leading-[1.06] tracking-[-.02em] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]" %}
{% set bodyp = "mt-5 text-[1.05rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[1180px] [&_a]:text-spark [&_a:hover]:underline [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold" %}
{% set btnfire = "btn h-auto min-h-0 rounded-full border-0 px-[1.4rem] py-[.85rem] font-smono text-[.78rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-[.05em] text-[#221302] bg-gradient-to-br from-spark via-flame to-ember hover:from-spark hover:via-flame hover:to-ember shadow-[0_6px_26px_-8px_rgba(232,145,43,.55)]" %}
{% set btnline = "btn btn-ghost h-auto min-h-0 rounded-full px-[1.4rem] py-[.85rem] font-smono text-[.78rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-[.05em] text-ink border border-ink/15 bg-ink/[0.03] hover:border-flame hover:text-spark hover:bg-ink/[0.03] normal-case" %}

<div class="relative overflow-x-clip bg-night text-ink font-body leading-[1.55] antialiased selection:bg-ember selection:text-[#160c02]">
  <div class="v2-ambient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="relative z-[1]">

    {# ===== header ===== #}
    <header class="pt-10 pb-2.5">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="mb-[26px] font-smono text-[.7rem] tracking-[.08em] uppercase text-ink-3"><a class="hover:text-spark" href="/">Bonfire</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><a class="hover:text-spark" href="/start">Set up &amp; host</a><span class="mx-2">/</span>Cooperative Hosting Network</p>
      <h1 class="font-disp font-semibold text-[clamp(2.1rem,5vw,3.7rem)] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-.02em] max-w-[17ch] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">Cooperative <span class="fire-text">Hosting Network.</span></h1>
      <p class="mt-[18px] font-disp font-normal text-[clamp(1.15rem,2.2vw,1.6rem)] leading-[1.3] text-ink max-w-[46ch]">An open invitation to assemble a co-operative ecosystem to operate a sustainable, resilient infrastructure for Bonfire development, hosting, and technical support.</p>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">You shouldn't have to become a sysadmin to own your community's space, nor hand it to a Big Tech landlord. <a class="underline decoration-ink/30 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-spark hover:text-spark" href="/self-hosting">Self-hosting</a> promises autonomy, but a community fending entirely for itself often just means renting from some giant's cloud, each instance idling away rare-earth minerals and energy that sharing would spare. What matters is who governs, not where the machines sit. So there's a third path between running everything yourself and paying a SaaS landlord: <b>shared, community-owned infrastructure</b>. That's what the Cooperative Hosting Network is for.</p>
    </div></header>

    {# ===== hosting partners — get hosted today + join ===== #}
    <section class="py-14 border-t border-ink/[0.07]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-corn">Hosting partners</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[26ch]">Get hosted today, <span class="font-light">or help build the network.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">While the wider cooperative network is still taking shape, partners in the cooperative ecosystem already run Bonfire instances. It's a joint effort with Co-op Cloud and CoQuest, with more co-ops and providers in conversation, and we're looking for others to join.</p>

      {% set partner = "block text-center group" %}
      {% set partnerimg = "w-full aspect-square rounded-xl object-cover border border-ink/15 bg-night-2 group-hover:border-flame/40" %}
      {% set partnername = "mt-3 font-disp font-[620] text-base text-ink" %}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 min-[821px]:grid-cols-4 gap-4 min-[821px]:gap-6 mt-8">
        <div class="text-center">
          <a class="{{ partner }}" href="https://coopcloud.tech/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <img class="{{ partnerimg }}" src="/img/coopcloud.png" alt="Co-op Cloud" loading="lazy" class="bg-[#f6f6f1] w-full aspect-square rounded-xl object-contain p-8">
            <div class="{{ partnername }}">Co-op Cloud</div>
          </a>
          <a class="mt-1.5 inline-block font-smono text-[.68rem] text-spark hover:underline" href="https://docs.coopcloud.tech/intro/managed/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Co-ops offering managed hosting →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <a class="{{ partner }}" href="https://coquest.coop/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {# svg logo: object-contain + padding instead of the photo treatment #}
            <img src="/img/coquest.svg" alt="CoQuest" loading="lazy" class="bg-[#f6f6f1] w-full aspect-square rounded-xl object-contain p-8">
            <div class="{{ partnername }}">CoQuest</div>
          </a>
          <a class="mt-1.5 inline-block font-smono text-[.68rem] text-spark hover:underline" href="https://coquest.coop/en/#contact" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get in touch →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <a class="{{ partner }}" href="/contact">
            <div class="w-full aspect-square rounded-xl border border-dashed border-ink/20 bg-night-2 flex items-center justify-center group-hover:border-flame/40">
              <span class="font-disp font-light text-[2.6rem] leading-none text-ink-3 group-hover:text-spark">+</span>
            </div>
            <div class="{{ partnername }}">Become a partner</div>
          </a>
          <a class="mt-1.5 inline-block font-smono text-[.68rem] text-spark hover:underline" href="/contact">Offer hosting or services →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== the model ===== #}
    <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame">The model</p>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">We're looking for more participants to join in building a sustainable and resilient cooperative hosting ecosystem in the face of digital landscapes dominated by profit-driven giants. Our model, inspired by Open Cooperative Ecosystems and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Community-supported_agriculture" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Community Supported Agriculture (CSA)</a>, treats the software, the infrastructure it runs on, and the communities that use it as parts of one system that sustains itself. We see it as a way to keep not-for-profit free software projects alive, while avoiding the traps of SaaS (software as a service) or other models.</p>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">Such a cooperative alliance brings together many kinds of people, all pitching in: users, communities, moderators, tech supporters, infrastructure operators, translators, designers, developers, and more. Participation and contribution can come in various forms: financial support, resource sharing, labour, and active participation in decision-making and project upkeep.</p>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">This approach based on solidarity and mutual aid would ensure resiliency, accessibility and diversity, while promoting open community involvement. It puts trust, transparency, and people's control over their own tools back at the heart of how the software gets made.</p>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">The Cooperative Hosting Network would greatly simplify the setup, hosting, and operation of a Bonfire instance through an automated install wizard and dashboard, which would act as a gateway to an ecosystem of developers, designers, hosting providers, and other relevant services, which would work together to provide users and communities with:</p>

      {# the four values #}
      {% set val = "grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-3.5 rounded-xl border border-ink/15 bg-night-2 p-[18px]" %}
      {% set valb = "w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] bg-flame [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" %}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[761px]:grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 mt-8">
        <div class="{{ val }}"><span class="{{ valb }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="font-disp font-semibold block mb-[3px] text-base">Openness</b><span class="text-ink-2 text-[.95rem]">Designers, developers, and sysadmins, among other workers, can join the ecosystem to provide services and receive compensation.</span></div></div>
        <div class="{{ val }}"><span class="{{ valb }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="font-disp font-semibold block mb-[3px] text-base">Mutualism</b><span class="text-ink-2 text-[.95rem]">Participants that meet specific criteria may exchange services in-kind, and benefit from special rates or pro-bono services.</span></div></div>
        <div class="{{ val }}"><span class="{{ valb }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="font-disp font-semibold block mb-[3px] text-base">Flexibility</b><span class="text-ink-2 text-[.95rem]">From a personal instance to a large community, the hosting ecosystem will guide the user based on their specific needs and budget.</span></div></div>
        <div class="{{ val }}"><span class="{{ valb }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="font-disp font-semibold block mb-[3px] text-base">Inclusivity</b><span class="text-ink-2 text-[.95rem]">Users and communities can collectively shape the ecosystem's roadmaps, by co-designing and funding desired features.</span></div></div>
      </div>

      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">The dashboard would also double as a decentralized economic network, transparently recording every contribution and distributing funds based on value equations democratically defined by the ecosystem stakeholders.</p>

    </div></section>

    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7 pb-16">
      <div class="relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink/15 max-w-[720px] mx-auto">
        <img class="w-full max-h-[220px] object-cover block" src="/img/mush.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-[linear-gradient(to_top,rgba(12,14,21,.55),transparent_40%)]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
